# T28 — Phase 4 — Anchor extractor + resolver (paths, symbols, errors, commands, APIs, config keys)

**Phase:** 4
**Type:** backend
**Model class:** balanced
**Depends on:** R26, T27
**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 4: Retrieval V1](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-4-retrieval-v1), [§Retrieval Engine](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#7-retrieval-engine), [§Phase 1: Unified Identity Model](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-1-unified-identity-model)
**Standards:** Cadres coding standard (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md`); Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).

## Goal

This task delivers steps 2 and 3 of the spec's retrieval pipeline: extract every literal anchor a user statement provides — file paths, symbol names, error strings, shell commands, API names, config keys — and resolve each into a stable graph identity using the Phase 1 identity resolver. Anchor resolution is the deterministic core of the pipeline; everything downstream (candidate retrieval, scoring, expansion handles) relies on the resolver returning canonical identities. Ambiguity must be surfaced, not hidden — the resolver returns the candidate set with disambiguation reasons so the scorer in T30 can weigh them and the diagnostic mode in T30/T36 can explain why each candidate was kept.

## Spec excerpts that drive this task

> "Pipeline: ... 2. Extract literal anchors: paths, symbols, errors, commands, APIs, config keys. 3. Resolve anchors into graph identities." (spec §7. Retrieval Engine)

> "Phase 4: Retrieval V1 — Deliverables: ... anchor extractor and resolver; hybrid candidate retrieval from graph, docs, memories, and events ..." (spec §Phase 4: Retrieval V1)

> "Phase 1: Unified Identity Model — Deliverables: stable IDs for files, symbols, doc sections, events, memories, and follow-up handles; identity resolver with ambiguity diagnostics ..." (spec §Phase 1: Unified Identity Model)

## Inputs

- Dependency outputs:
  - R26 verdict — confirms the Phase 3 memory graph (including link tables and identity references) is stable.
  - T27 `IntentClassification` — anchor extraction is biased by intent (debug tasks prioritize error/stack-trace anchors; refactor tasks prioritize symbol anchors; docs tasks prioritize section/heading anchors).
- Existing files in the repo this task builds on:
  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/` (Phase 1 deliverable; provides the resolver T28 calls).
  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/graph/` (`SymbolId`, file nodes, doc section nodes — the identities resolution targets).
  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/intent.rs` (T27) — supplies the `IntentClassification` input.
- Standards files to honor: `/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md` (single source of truth — call the identity resolver, do not reimplement path normalization); `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md` (Markdown heading references where behaviour is doc-anchored).

## Steps

1. Re-read spec §Retrieval Engine pipeline steps 2 and 3, and §Phase 1 identity resolver deliverable, so the inputs and outputs are aligned with the existing identity model.
2. Design the anchor taxonomy in a doc-comment table at the top of `anchors.rs`: `PathAnchor`, `SymbolAnchor`, `ErrorAnchor` (with optional stack frames), `CommandAnchor`, `ApiAnchor` (HTTP routes, RPC methods, MCP tool names), `ConfigKeyAnchor`. Each variant declares the regex/token shape it matches and the identity family it resolves to.
3. Implement `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/anchors.rs`: pure-function extractor `extract_anchors(task_text: &str, intent: &IntentClassification) -> Vec<RawAnchor>` and resolver `resolve_anchors(raws: Vec<RawAnchor>, resolver: &IdentityResolver) -> Vec<ResolvedAnchor>`. Resolution returns the canonical identity, the candidate set when ambiguous, the ambiguity reason, and the source span in the task text.
4. Route every path normalization, symbol lookup, and doc-section lookup through the existing Phase 1 `IdentityResolver` API — do not reimplement these in `anchors.rs` (single source of truth per `coding.md`).
5. Bias extraction by intent: for `debug` intent, raise the error/stack-frame regex priority and accept commonly-occurring error idioms (`thread 'X' panicked at ...`, `error[E\d+]:`, `Traceback (most recent call last):`); for `refactor`/`add_feature`/`modify_feature`, raise symbol-name extraction; for `update_docs`, raise Markdown heading and `path/to/file.md#heading` anchor extraction. Document the bias rules inline with `## Retrieval Engine` heading citation.
6. Emit a `diagnostics()` view on `ResolvedAnchor` returning `(anchor_text, resolved_identity, ambiguity_reason, source_span)` so the scorer (T30) can apply `exact identifier match` weighting and the diagnostic mode can show why an anchor was matched or skipped.
7. Add `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/anchors_tests.rs` covering: each anchor variant detected in canonical inputs; intent bias rerouting (debug inputs surface errors first); ambiguous symbol names return the full candidate set with reason; unknown paths resolve to a `PathAnchor::Unresolved` rather than panicking; resolver round-trip preserves source spans; serde round-trip for the diagnostics view; empty input returns an empty vector without panic.
8. Run `cd daemon && cargo build --release` and the verification test command; fix any clippy warnings before stopping.

## Files expected

- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/anchors.rs` — anchor taxonomy, extractor, resolver, diagnostics view.
- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/anchors_tests.rs` — in-tree tests for extraction, resolution, intent bias, ambiguity, and diagnostics.

## Verification

- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/anchors.rs` — confirms the extractor/resolver module exists at the expected path.
- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib retrieval_v1::anchors_tests` — runs the in-tree tests and asserts every anchor variant, intent bias, and ambiguity case is covered.

## Coding-standard checks

- File length ≤800 lines per file.
- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10. Extraction is table-driven (regex/feature table) rather than nested match blocks.
- Schema parity: not applicable (no SQL in this task).
- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code, or unjustified `#[allow(...)]`.
- Single source of truth: identity resolution is delegated to the Phase 1 `IdentityResolver`; no duplicated path/symbol normalization in this module.
- No broken windows: dead imports removed, every public name expresses intent.
- Doc citation: comments describing behaviour mandated by `## 7. Retrieval Engine` or `## Phase 1: Unified Identity Model` cite those exact headings per `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`.

## Definition of done

- [ ] Every file in "Files expected" exists with real content (no stubs).
